We consider $n$ independent pairs $(X_i,Y_i) \sim F_{XY}^{(w)}(x,y)$ of scalar continuous random variables, sampled from the joint density
\begin{equation}
f^{(w)}_{X,Y}(x,y)={w}(x,y) f_{XY}(x,y)/\mathbb{E}_{f_{XY}} \{{w}(X,Y)\},
\label{eq:weighted_density}
\end{equation}
where ${w} : \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}^+$ is a non-negative weight function such that $0 < \mathbb{E}_{f_{XY}}\{{w}(X,Y)\} < \infty$.

\begin{equation}
f^{(w)}_{X,Y}(x,y)={w}(x,y) f_{XY}(x,y)/\mathbb{E}_{f_{XY}} \{{w}(X,Y)\},
\label{eq:weighted_density}
\end{equation}

An important special case is that of a truncated sample in which

\begin{align}
	{w}(x,y) = \setindicator{\mathcal{A}}(x,y) = \left\{ \begin{array}{lll}
	1  &   \quad (x,y) \in \mathcal{A}  \\
	0 & \quad otherwise, \\
	\end{array} \right.
	\label{eq:truncation_function}
\end{align}	

for some set $\mathcal{A} \subset \mathbb{R}^2$.

